### Corrective Actions Implemented



**Each command targets the physical cause of the defect**

| Defect | Commands issued | Physical rationale |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Over-extrusion** | `M104 S190`, `M220 S95`, `M221 S80` | Lower melt flow and volumetric delivery; stabilise deposition

 |
| **Under-extrusion** | `M104 S205`, `M220 S80`, `M221 S110` | Reduce melt viscosity, give the extruder more time, raise multiplier

 |
| **Stringing** | `M104 S190`, `M220 S80`, `M221 S95` | Limit oozing and filament pressure during travel moves

 |
| **Warping** | `M140 S65` | Raise bed temperature to restore adhesion and reduce contraction

 |
| **Clog / Layer shift / Spaghetti** | `M112` emergency stop | Further printing risks damage; correction is not attempted

 |

> A severity-dependent action policy already exists. What it lacks is a stated envelope and a justification.
> 
> 

