### The Mechanical Proposal – A Four-Layer Safety Gate



**Turning one emergency stop into a stated operating envelope**

```
[ AI recommendation ]
(Δ setpoint + explanation)
         │
         ▼
[ L1 Physical limits ] ───► Motor, heater and drive limits from machine's spec
 (torque · speed · temp · pressure)
         │
         ▼
[ L2 Rate and step limits ] ───► Maximum change per cycle (prevents overshoot/oscillation)
 (maximum Δ per cycle)
         │
         ▼
[ L3 Process window ] ───► Region actually characterised by design of experiments
 (region actually characterised)
         │
         ▼
[ L4 Confidence gate ] ───► Act only when uncertainty is below threshold; else escalate
 (uncertainty below threshold)
         │
         ▼
〈 All four passed? 〉
  │              │
 PASS           FAIL
  │              │
  ▼              ▼
[ Apply, or propose ]   [ Hold and escalate ]
[   to operator     ]   [    to a human     ]

```

> Same logic as CARR's actuation-authority work on legged robots, applied to process setpoints.
> 
> 

